{"term":"vanish","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:855c7cb66a04d6fae6","definition":"To become invisible or to move out of view unnoticed.","example":"Holly, mistletoe, red berries, ivy, turkeys, geese, game, poultry, brawn, meat, pigs, sausages, oysters, pies, puddings, fruit, and punch, all vanished instantly.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disappear"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["angle of vanishing stability","Kodaira vanishing theorem","vanishable","vanisher","vanishing foam","vanishing fraction","vanishing ideal","vanishing point","vanishing spray","vanishing testes syndrome","vanishing twin","vanishing twin syndrome","vanish into thin air","vanish to the four winds"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:82b1f0b85df73fa4a7","definition":"To become equal to zero.","example":"The function f such as f(x)#61;x² vanishes at x#61;0.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disappear"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["angle of vanishing stability","Kodaira vanishing theorem","vanishable","vanisher","vanishing foam","vanishing fraction","vanishing ideal","vanishing point","vanishing spray","vanishing testes syndrome","vanishing twin","vanishing twin syndrome","vanish into thin air","vanish to the four winds"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanish#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:03ab04a83429482b2f","definition":"To disappear; to kidnap.","example":"And as if to prove it, one of his friends was vanished and was never seen again. The guy got in a taxi one night, and no one ever saw him ever again.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disappear"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["angle of vanishin